Tries

A trie is a specialized tree based data structure used to store and retrieve keys efficently in a dataset of strings

A trie breaks down words into indiciidual cahracters and shares common prefixes amound them


for example is you stire the words

"CAT" "CAR" and "CART"

Then the trie reuses them into a shared "CA" path for all three words.
"THe root node in the top of the tree is always empty and does not hold a character"

The edges and child nodes there each is a path or a link downward wich represents a specific character


End of a word Flag has a node which contains a boolean flag and this differtiates a standalone word form a prefix 


The advantage of a trie is speed and there is a fast look up time and no hash collision. There is prefix mathcinging so it can instantly pull all words starting with a specific seuence 

There is a trade-off Memory. As tries are incredibliy fast so they can be highly space-inefficent. Every single node requites pointers or look up tables to manange its potnetial child letters.

